{"mode":"training","language":"en","altTextLanguage":"","title":"","instruction":{"english":"","german":""},"allowInstructionLineBreaks":false,"readingText":{"instruction":{"german":"","english":""},"content":"","configs":[]},"sequences":[{"instruction":{"german":"<p>Read the conversation in Figure it out and complete the rules in the grammar box.<\/p>","english":""},"configs":[{"correctAnswer":"Have","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_2","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_9\/p119_ex1\/"},{"correctAnswer":"Has","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_3","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_9\/p119_ex1\/"},{"correctAnswer":"have","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_4","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_9\/p119_ex1\/"},{"correctAnswer":"haven't","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_5","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_9\/p119_ex1\/"},{"correctAnswer":"never","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_6","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_9\/p119_ex1\/"}],"staticConfigs":[{"table":[["<p><sup>1<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_2\"><\/gap><\/p>","<p>I<\/p><p>we<\/p><p>they<\/p><p>you<\/p>","<p class=\"ql-align-center ql-direction-rtl\">(ever)<\/p>","<p>been to the capital city?<\/p><p>played a board game?<\/p><p>listened to old music?<\/p>"],["<p><sup>2<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_3\"><\/gap><\/p>","<p>he <\/p><p>she<\/p><p>it<\/p>","<p><br><\/p>","<p><br><\/p>"]],"border":"1px solid white","cellWidths":[100,100,100,100],"id":"custom-table_0","type":"custom-table"}],"parts":["<p><b>Figure it out<\/b><\/p><p><b>A:<\/b> Have you ever been to the USA?<\/p><p><b>B:<\/b> Yes, I have.<\/p><p><b>A:<\/b> Have you ever visited New York?<\/p><p><b>B:<\/b> No, I haven\u2019t. I\u2019ve never been to New York. Only Miami.<\/p><p><b>Grammar | Present perfect questions<\/b><\/p><p>We use the present perfect to ask about experiences in the past.<\/p><p>\u2022 We can use ever in questions.<\/p><p><em>Ever<\/em> = \u2018in your life\u2019.<\/p><p><custom-table id=\"custom-table_0\"><\/custom-table><\/p><p>\u2022 The short answer is <em>Yes, I<\/em> <sup>3<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_4\"><\/gap> or <em>No, I<\/em> <sup>4<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_5\"><\/gap>.<\/p><p>\u2022 We can use <sup>5<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_6\"><\/gap> in negatives.<\/p><p><em>Never<\/em> = \u2018not ever\u2019. When we use never, we don\u2019t use not.<\/p><p><em>I\u2019ve never been to England. <\/em>(not <em><s>I\u2019ve never not been to England.<\/s><\/em>)<\/p>"],"globalTypesConfigs":[{"type":"gap","widthMode":"asLongestWord","longestAlternativeSolutions":false,"ignoreCaseSensitivity":false}],"staticText":{"text":"<p><br><\/p>","backgroundColor":"lightgray","isSet":false}}]}